course: dictionary
lesson: 5222
title: Mild words for surprise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are cries. They show a feeling in one quick burst, like a shout. Jeepers is one of these. It is an interjection, and it shows surprise. «"Jeepers" is an old-fashioned American mild word used instead of "Jesus".» The clue is in the words "mild" and "instead of": it is a softer word people use in place of a stronger one.
explain: Context tells you the feeling. Read the words near it. If someone says «"Jeepers!" when the lid flew off the box», the surprise is in the sudden event, not in a long story. You do not need to know who or what is involved to see that the speaker is startled.
explain: Why swap a word? Some people do not want to use a holy name or a rude word, even when they feel strongly. A mild word lets them show the feeling without causing offence. Old films, cartoons and older people often use words like this, sometimes as a joke.
fact: An interjection is a short word or phrase that shows a feeling, like surprise or pain.
fact: «Jeepers» means a cry of surprise or shock.
fact: «Jeepers» is a mild stand-in for «Jesus», so people use it without saying the stronger word.
fact: «Jeepers» is old-fashioned and mainly American, and you may also hear it in Australia.
fact: «Jeepers» is often heard in old films and cartoons, and older people sometimes say it jokingly.
exercise: «"Jeepers!" cried Mia, when the dog jumped out of the box.» What does jeepers show? | *Surprise | Anger about the dog | Tiredness | Hunger
exercise: «"Jeepers" is an old-fashioned American mild word used instead of "Jesus".» Why do people use jeepers instead of Jesus? | *To show surprise without using a holy name | To ask for help | To count | To say goodbye
exercise: Where is jeepers mainly heard? | Canada | Scotland | Wales | *The United States
test: Jayden says, «Jeepers, I didn't see that coming!» What feeling does jeepers show? | Anger | *Surprise | Sleepiness | Hunger
test: Which word does jeepers stand in for? | Jumpers | *Jesus | Creepers | Jeeps
exam: Which sentence about jeepers is true? | Jeepers means a type of car | *Jeepers is a mild cry of surprise, used instead of a stronger word | Jeepers is a modern slang word for sleep | Jeepers is a kind of petrol station
